Scaling, Architecture, Design & UX Guidelines
Scaling Principles (Lean for 1M Users as Solo Founder)
Build Memark to auto-scale from 0 to 1M users without manual ops—focus on serverless, low-cost, monitorable stack. Start small (free tiers for MVP), optimize for high read/write (1M saves/month = ~30k/day). Key:

User Growth Handling: Supabase Pro ($25/mo base, auto-scales to 100k MAU included, then ~$0.003/MAU). Twilio toll-free/shared number for trial (3 MPS throughput, cheap $2/mo + $0.01/msg; upgrade to dedicated long-code for pro users at $1-2/extra/mo, charge premium).
Cost Control: Monitor via Supabase dashboard (usage alerts for DB/storage ~8GB included, egress 250GB). AI credits (OpenAI/Grok) ~$0.01/query—cap per user in basic tier. Total at 1M users: ~$5k/mo (scale with revenue from $9.99/19.99 tiers).
Performance: Lazy load previews/images (CDN via Supabase storage), cache AI categorizations (Supabase edge functions with TTL). Offline support (AsyncStorage for recent items). Rate limit Twilio to prevent spam (strict phone-ID rule).
Monitoring/Lean Ops: Use Supabase logs + Stripe dashboards (webhooks for plans). Add Mixpanel for usage (free tier to 100k events/mo). No dedicated ops—automate alerts (email/SMS via Twilio for critical thresholds).
Future-Proof: Design for 1M from start (row-level security everywhere, batch jobs for refreshes). If hits 1M, swap to AWS Lambda for custom scale (but keep Supabase for DB).

Architecture (Lean, Serverless, Cross-Platform)
Minimal stack for solo build/maintenance: Expo/React Native (mobile + web code share 80%), Supabase (DB/auth/storage/realtime/edge functions), Twilio (SMS). No custom servers—everything serverless.

Frontend: Expo/React Native for iOS/Android (haptics, share-sheet), Next.js for web (SSR for SEO, PWA support). Shared components (ItemCard, ProfileScreen) for consistency.
Backend: Supabase Postgres (items/profiles/users tables, RLS strict per user), edge functions (categorize-item for AI/previews, batch_refresh_previews, webhook for Twilio).
Integration Flow: Inbound SMS/share → webhook (strict phone-ID lookup) → save item → AI + preview fetch → realtime update feed (Supabase subscriptions).
Data Model: Users (phone primary ID, plan_type), Items (user_id, type, preview_title/desc/image/url), Profiles (user_id, public_marks array, opt-in).
Security/Compliance: Twilio Verify on signup, RLS (auth.uid() = user_id), encrypt sensitive (notes). GDPR ready (user data export/delete in Settings).
Deployment: Expo EAS for mobile builds (free for dev, $29/mo pro), Vercel for web (free for MVP, scales auto). GitHub Actions for CI/CD.

Design & UX (Award-Winning, Cohesive, Consistent)
Minimal Notion-like vibe: Purple palette (#8B5CF6 primary, #EC4899 accents, white/black neutrals), ample white space, Inter/SF Pro fonts, subtle shadows/gradients for depth. Everything consistent (icons/buttons/animations across platforms), easy nav (bottom tabs + swipe gestures), industry standards (responsive, accessible, performant).

Cohesiveness: Unified theme.ts (colors/fonts/spacing/haptics). All screens tie to "vault" metaphor (secure, organized, revisit-focused).
Consistency: Standard patterns (expandable ItemCard for previews/links, haptics on every interaction: tap/open/share/refresh). Dark/light modes auto-switch. Icons: Custom purple line SVGs (replace all multi-color — fork for recipes, etc.).
Easy Navigation: Bottom tabs (Feed, Collections, Search, Profile, Settings) — Framer Motion/Reanimated for smooth transitions. Global search bar, back gestures, keyboard shortcuts on web.
UX Standards: WCAG 2.1 access (contrast 4.5:1, screen reader labels, voiceover for haptics). Fast load (skeletons + lazy images). Haptics/feedback on all actions. Offline mode (view recent items). Personalization (pro custom themes/icons).
Visual Polish: Award-winning minimalism (no clutter, 3D M logo variants for splash). Previews/badges in cards (𝕏 for X, ▶ for YouTube). Browser: Stay in app (mobile WebView, web iframe/overlay).

Build lean: Prioritize core (capture/AI/feed) → add sharing/profiles → monetize. Test visuals in Expo preview after every change (expo start --clear). This sets Memark for 1M users as one-person SAAS! 🚀2.2sExpert